ly true  the risk of course is  that  because there's no republican in the  presidential debates  very few republicans even watch it you  have a democrat with a couple of  third-party candidates and all it serves  to do  is to siphon off some voters from the  democratic candidate to those  third-party candidates so i think it is  not a strategy without risk it would  absolutely trigger republicans to be  left out for sure  it might be to their benefit and so i  think it has to be thought through  very carefully  harb wrote in with an idea  for a different five-day work week now  we've been talking a lot about the  four-day work week the four-day work  week the idea is you have a four-day  work week and a three-day weekend every  week you do a little bit of adjustment  of hours you do a little bit of  adjustment of expectations and you sort  of like more or less get the same amount  of work done in information type jobs  knowledge jobs this doesn't work when  it's about a retail store being open as  you would in a five-day work week harp  has a different idea which is a five day  work week  which is  three days on two days off so the  weekends move and the idea would be you  do three 10 hour days and then you get  two days off  and then you get another three ten hour  days and then you get two days off so  the two days off shift throughout the  week it's a little complicated but the  idea is  that you end up working  a little more each year but you also  have more days off each year and this  will allow people to have both weekdays  off and weekends off i think it's really  interesting and there's a lot of sense  in it and i've heard proposals like this  before  the difficulty is it does become a  nightmare for child care it becomes a  nightmare for a lot of different things  where you have to know okay if i'm  making a doctor's appointment for six  months in advance is this the week where  i have wednesday and thursday off or is  this the week where i have saturday 